2-regularity of solutions to the Poisson equation 
  \begin{equation*}
  \begin{cases}
  \Delta \, u = f & \text{ in } \Omega, \\
  u = g & \text{ on } \partial \Omega,
  \end{cases}
  \end{cases}
  \noindent over unbounded domains with regular boundaries in $\mathbb{R}^n$ for $n\geq 3$.  We define a specific scale of domains named $\lambda$-exterior domains and establish that on such domains, the $\dot{W}^{2,p}$ solvability of the given boundary value problem holds within bounded subdomains.  Conversely, we prove the necessity of this condition for the $\dot{W}^{2,p}$ solvability of the problem.  As a result, it follows that the set of admissible exponents for the $\dot{W}^{2,p}$ solvability of the given boundary value problem on external domains in $\mathbb{R}^n$ is precisely $(1, \infty)$.  Our findings further allow us to recover recent outcomes obtained by Deringer and Kalton, in addition to providing insights into open questions raised by Deringer and others.
